  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h3 id="khp3" class="h1">Khp 3.  Dvattiṁsākāra — The 32 Parts</h3>
            <p><em>In this body there is:</em></p>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>hair of the head, hair of the body,</p>
              <p>nails, teeth, skin,</p>
              <p>muscle, tendons,</p>
              <p>bones, bone marrow,</p>
              <p>spleen, heart, liver,</p>
              <p>membranes, kidneys, lungs,</p>
              <p>large intestines, small intestines,</p>
              <p>gorge, feces,</p>
              <p>gall, phlegm, lymph, blood,</p>
              <p>sweat, fat, tears, oil,</p>
              <p>saliva, mucus, oil in the joints, urine,</p>
              <p class="v1">brain in the skull.<span class="fn"><a href="#khp3note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
            </div>
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="khp3note01">1. This item is not usually included in the list of the parts of the body in other parts of the Canon, such as <a href="../../DN/DN22.html">DN 22</a>, <a href="../../MN/MN10.html">MN 10</a>, and <a href="../../MN/MN119.html">MN 119</a>. Its presence here suggests that this passage—and perhaps the whole of Khp—was assembled during the time of the Commentaries, which unlike DN and MN, include the brain in the list.</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
            <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../../DN/DN22.html">DN 22</a>; <a href="../../MN/MN119.html">MN 119</a>; <a href="../../SN/SN54_9.html">SN 54:9</a>; <a href="../../AN/AN7_48.html">AN 7:48</a>; <a href="../../AN/AN4_163.html">AN 4:163</a>; <a href="../../AN/AN9_15.html">AN 9:15</a>; <a href="../../AN/AN10_60.html">AN 10:60</a>; <a href="../Dhp/Ch11.html#dhp147">Dhp 147–150</a>; <a href="../StNp/StNp1_11.html">Sn 1:11</a>; <a href="../StNp/StNp5_16.html">Sn 5:16</a>; <a href="../Thag/thag10_5.html">Thag 10:5</a>; <a href="../Thig/thig13_1.html">Thig 13:1</a>; <a href="../Thig/thig14.html">Thig 14</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
